Use of AI tools
AI tools were used throughout this work; responsibility for all of it rests with the authors. AI coding
assistants (Anthropic’s Claude models) wrote most of the simulator, analysis, test and release code to
the authors’ specifications, and drafted parts of the text; the authors set the research questions, the
registered hypotheses, decision rules and every amendment, and checked and revised all text. Two
attackers involve language models by design: H1 is a language model acting as the focal provider,
and H4 was written by a fresh session of an OpenAI model, started by the authors, against the
frozen defenders (Appendix F). Drafts of the protocol, code and paper were reviewed by OpenAI
GPT models and by Claude, read-only; each correction was checked against the repository before
it was adopted. No AI tool is an author.


